{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/872695-x20-damn-that-s-a-lot-of-rolling","id":872695,"title":"X20: Damn, that's a lot of rolling...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-23T15:54:48-07:00","id":872695,"title":"X20: Damn, that's a lot of rolling...","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Anyone using any dice house rules they're finding helpful to cut down on the amount of rolling in the X20 games? It's been years since I've played the system and I completely forgot the absurd amount of rolling involved. Four rolls per attack. Yikes.<br /> <br /> So what are some dice and rolling hacks people are using?<br /> <br /> Anything like...<br /> <br /> Making the difficulty of resisted/opposed rolls the target's dice pool total. You attack, they dodge. Okay, so your difficulty to attack is now their dodge dice pool. Done. One roll.<br /> <br /> Taking average rolls. Declare the difficulty is always 6, acknowledge that you'll get--on average--one success for every two dice rolled. And just declare average successes based on dice pool size. Any maths people know the averages for successes at different difficulties? Maybe we could get a chart? Or if there are any ANYDICE experts, perhaps a formula for same?<br /> <br /> Any tricks from the nWoD games useful for porting to the X20 line? I haven't played any so I honestly don't know. Any help would be awesome.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T17:11:28-07:00","id":872744,"title":"","content":"Trying to port in ChroD mechanics would probably result in something not so great. Some other developments the more compatible iterations of the ST system have done, however, might be.<br /> <br /> - Soak could automatic like in the Aeon Continuum games or Exalted; bashing is equal to Stamina, lethal equal to half that, rounded down. Some tougher characters types might retain full Stamina soak for lethal damage as well.<br /> - Defense could be automatic like in Exalted since 2e. Half the total of your Attribute + Ability pool, rounded up. Ex2 gave ties to defense, but Ex3 allows you to hit for 0 successes added to damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T22:52:44-07:00","id":872907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/872695-x20-damn-that-s-a-lot-of-rolling?p=872744#post872744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soak could automatic like in the Aeon Continuum games or Exalted; bashing is equal to Stamina, lethal equal to half that, rounded down. Some tougher characters types might retain full Stamina soak for lethal damage as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could certainly work. Stamina would basically become armor then. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Defense could be automatic like in Exalted since 2e. Half the total of your Attribute + Ability pool, rounded up. Ex2 gave ties to defense, but Ex3 allows you to hit for 0 successes added to damage. </div> </div> </div>Sure, could work.<br /> <br /> You could also combine them. Take the dodge pool plus stamina, divide by 2, and round down. That's how many successes you have to beat in your to-hit roll to actually cause damage. And it's all in one roll. 1:1 success:damage from there. But that is terribly offset toward the defender. Maybe dex + stamina / 2, round down...<br /> <br /> Two combat monkeys with 5 dots in all the relevant traits. Attacker rolls 10 dice vs diff 6. That's an average of five successes. A defender that gets +athletics has a threshold of 7 successes to cause damage. A defender that gets dex + stamina has a threshold of 5 successes to cause damage. It's balanced at least. <br /> <br /> But a success threshold is functionally equivalent to a higher difficulty. So your auto defenses roughly work out to be the same as my attacker's difficulty = defender's dice pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T20:53:52-07:00","id":875220,"title":"","content":"In the WoD Streetfighter game for combat, you took the lower pool out of the higher pool's # of dice, so if i had 8 dice to hit you with, and you had 5 to dodge/block, i would only roll 3, and if those came up, i hit/damaged you... Same was done with damage/soak..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T22:05:37-07:00","id":875281,"title":"","content":"That's bizarre. So it assumes all the defender's dice will succeed, but the attacker still has to roll. <br /> <br /> I think that's part of my problem with WoD combat. It's set up so that it's basically roll till you fail. Four rolls just to inflict some damage on a target. Roll to-hit, roll to defend, roll to damage, roll to soak. It's a whole lot of rolling <i>every action</i>... just to do a little bit of damage, maybe. I know, I know. Lopsided combat and all that. Still doesn't make handling the system any easier.<br /> <br /> Actually, the quick and dirty combat setup from God Machine Chronicle looks absolutely perfect. Declare intent/goal, assemble a dice pool, and roll. Winner gets their goal and the loser takes damage equal to the winner's successes (if applicable). One roll for the whole damn combat, not four rolls per action. Love that so much. And it's easy enough to scale to handle round-level goals for those really big, climactic fights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T00:02:14-07:00","id":875382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/872695-x20-damn-that-s-a-lot-of-rolling?p=875220#post875220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the WoD Streetfighter game for combat, you took the lower pool out of the higher pool's # of dice, so if i had 8 dice to hit you with, and you had 5 to dodge/block, i would only roll 3, and if those came up, i hit/damaged you... Same was done with damage/soak..</div> </div> </div> </div>There was no dodging or blocking in SF. Only soak, which auto-subtracted from damage in a way that ChroD would eventually use for non-soak defenses, as soak was rolled into having more health levels. There's a reason why they call it the SF: the Storytelling Game rather than the Storyteller game...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T09:33:20-07:00","id":876733,"title":"","content":"Might want to take a look <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/715707-the-slow-pacing-in-combat\">over here</a>, since this is a question that comes up frequently.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}